course: dictionary
lesson: 11486
title: Afghan: a person, a dog and a blanket
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants. «The Afghan hound ran across the park.» Here Afghan tells you the kind of dog, so it means a tall dog with long, silky hair.
explain: Capital letters help too. «Afghan food» has a capital A because Afghanistan is a country, so Afghan means from Afghanistan. «Grandma knitted an afghan for the sofa» has a small a, so it means a blanket.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. «My friend's family is Afghan.» Does it still make sense if you read it as "from Afghanistan"? Yes, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Afghan with a capital A can mean a person from Afghanistan, or from or to do with Afghanistan.
fact: An Afghan hound is a tall dog with long, silky hair.
fact: «Afghan» with a small a can mean a knitted or crocheted blanket, often colourful (US and Canada).
fact: An Afghan coat is an older UK word for a sheepskin coat with the woolly side inside.
fact: Afghanistan is a country in Central and South Asia.
exercise: «My friend's grandma is from Afghanistan, so she is an Afghan.» What is an Afghan? | A tall dog with silky hair | *A person from Afghanistan | A knitted blanket | A sheepskin coat
exercise: Grandma knitted a colourful «afghan» for the sofa. What is an afghan here? | *A knitted blanket | A kind of cake | A person from Afghanistan | A tall dog
exercise: «The Afghan hound ran across the park with its long hair flying.» What kind of animal is an Afghan hound? | *A dog | A rabbit | A cat | A horse
test: «We ate Afghan food for dinner, with rice and warm bread.» What does Afghan mean in «Afghan food»? | Made of wool | *From Afghanistan | Very spicy and hot | Cold and frozen
test: Which word is right for a blanket that Grandma knitted? | Afghanistan | *an afghan | an Afghan | an Afghan hound
exam: Which sentence uses the word correctly? | Grandma wrapped an Afghan hound around my legs on the sofa. | Grandma wrapped Afghanistan around my legs on the sofa. | *Grandma wrapped an afghan around my legs on the sofa. | Grandma wrapped an Afghan around my legs, because she was a dog.
